answer:
**Solution:**

John buys 5 notebooks, and each notebook has 40 pages. To find the total number of pages, we multiply the number of notebooks by the number of pages per notebook:

\[
\text{Total pages} = 5 \text{ notebooks} \times 40 \text{ pages/notebook} = 200 \text{ pages}
\]

John uses 4 pages per day. To determine how many days the notebooks will last, we divide the total number of pages by the number of pages used per day:

\[
\text{Number of days} = \frac{200 \text{ pages}}{4 \text{ pages/day}} = 50 \text{ days}
\]

**Answer:** \boxed{50}

